# Profile entry for dpv-odrl:Location over DPV Locations, the jurisdictional slice.
#
# The operand is dpv-odrl:Location, the DPV-ODRL left operand for places
# drawn from DPV. DPV-ODRL places it below odrl:spatial, the operand the
# GeoNames profile binds. The sort is mer in all three profiles. What
# differs between them is the resource: which file, and which of the
# relations in that file the binding reads.  That is what it means for the
# meaning to belong to the binding rather than to the operand.
#
# The resource is containment together with union membership,
# read as jurisdictional containment.  isPartOf EU has an answer
# here and does not under the territorial profile.  Neither is
# the correct reading of the file: they are two readings, and
# the profile is where the reading is stated.
#
# DPV writes identity with skos:sameAs, which is not a SKOS term (see
# https://github.com/w3c-cg/dpv/issues/485).  skos:sameAs and owl:sameAs
# are both read as identity.  DPV links BQ and SJ to several islands, BQ
# to NL-BQ1, NL-BQ2 and NL-BQ3 and SJ to NO-21 and NO-22, so this binding
# identifies those islands with one another.  No case relies on it.

@prefix dpv-odrl: <https://w3id.org/dpv/mappings/odrl#> .
@prefix bind: <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/binding#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/profile/> .

ex:b-spatial-dpvloc-juris a bind:OperandBinding ;
    rdfs:label "DPV Locations, jurisdictional reading: places and their parts"@en ;
    bind:leftOperand dpv-odrl:Location ;
    bind:sort bind:mer ;
    bind:resource <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/dpv-loc-juris> ;
    bind:grounding bind:sliceMembership .
